Z||000000||fiero56||12-28-2000||12:26 AM||||I have always been a big fan of the Muncie 4-speed(used with the v-6). One of my favorite things about the Muncie is the gearing on it. I don't mind shifting, but with this tranny, the shifts are spread much farter apart than with my Getrag 5-speed(also used with the v-6). With my Getrag, I have to pull second gear before I can even exit an intersection on a left turn. The Muncie is very nice for around town driving. My only gripe about the Muncie is it has no nice highway gear. This is where the Isuzu comes into the picture.<BR>The Isuzu tranny is very plentiful, can get ahold of them pretty cheap, and they have replaceable brass inside. I am wondering about the possibility of getting ahold of, the compatibility of, and usefullness of, getting new brass for the Isuzu to match the Muncie tranny. Specifically I would like to have the first 4 gears closely matching those of the Muncie 4-speed, and the 5th being a nice highway cruising gear. <P>Anybody know how realistic this is? Some idea of a cost, or if it is even a good idea? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Got2manyfieros||12-28-2000||01:21 AM||||Quaif manufactures different gear sets for that transmission...along wit high performance differentials.||||reg||1
